<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC meeting ends, agrees six month output freeze.</title>
<headline>OPEC meeting ends, agrees six month output freeze.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC ended its meeting here on Thursday with an agreement to freeze its 25.03 million barrels per day output ceiling for the first six months of next year, OPEC Secretary-General Rilwanu Lukman said.</p>
<p>Lukman added that the group would meet again in late June 1997.  </p>
<p>The six month rollover agreement had been widely anticipated. OPEC members' quotas were also unchanged, an OPEC delegate said.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
